# iPad / iPhone deploy / signing / backup

Canonical commands + Vietnamese notes:
- iPad: `ipad-app/Scripts/COMMANDS.md`
- iPhone: `iphone-app/Scripts/COMMANDS.md`

## What to use when

| Goal | Do this |
|------|---------|
| Code update on real iPad | `ipad-app/Scripts/deploy-ipad.sh` (`DEVICE_UDID` required). Fast incremental — **no clean**, no DerivedData wipe. |
| Code update on real iPhone | `iphone-app/Scripts/deploy-iphone.sh` (`DEVICE_UDID` required). Same rules as iPad. |
| Free cert / profile expiry (~7d) | iPad: `renew-ipad-signing.sh` · iPhone: `renew-iphone-signing.sh` (`DEVICE_UDID` + `TEAM`). Optional LaunchAgents every 12h. |
| Persist data across reinstall | In-app **Thư mục** / **Backup** / **Restore** → Google Drive via Files (`BackupService`, file `caption-studio-backup.json`). |
| First physical install | Manual Xcode Automatic Signing + Trust — see `FIRST_RUN.md` in each app’s `Scripts/`. |

## Hard rules

- **Never delete the app** on the device just to update or resign — that wipes the SwiftData sandbox. Overwrite install (same Bundle ID) only.
- Prefer deploy scripts for day-to-day code; prefer renew scripts for signing-only refresh.
- Wireless works after one pair: same Wi‑Fi, unlocked device, same `DEVICE_UDID`.
- UDID: `xcrun xctrace list devices` (or Xcode Devices → Identifier).
- Bundle IDs: iPad `com.example.YouTubeJPCaptionStudio` · iPhone `com.example.YouTubeJPCaptionStudio.iPhone` (install side by side).
